{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384826-homebrew-ideas-need-help-v5","id":1384826,"title":"Homebrew Ideas, Need Help [V5]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T05:50:29-07:00","id":1384826,"title":"Homebrew Ideas, Need Help [V5]","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My </span></span></span></div><i>Chicago By Night</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> chronicle is going to have its second session this Saturday, and already I'm starting to collect notes on how I want to run things going forward, namely not rolling randomly on the Compulsion table: one of my players had a bestial failure negotiating with Flyboy, I rolled on the table, oops got Hunger Compulsion and he's at 1 Hunger. So the next session is going to start with him, you know, killing someone. Thankfully my players picked &quot;Punish the wicked&quot; as a Chroncle Tenet, so I think their current plan is to stalk the streets until they can find an assault in progress and he can chow down with a relatively clean conscience. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My other idea is accolade XP: V5 had a near-identical XP cost table to VtR 1e, right down to the exponential XP costs. The VtR 1e rulebook includes a section on how to award XP, namely participating in the session, resolving the current objective in the chronicle well, uncovering important info, good RP, bravery, and coming up with cool or creative solutions to problems. I personally favor this solution, since my group plays once every other week, and a simple 1 or 2 XP per session just feels glacial, especially considering the exponential XP costs. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My other idea is about allowing my players to purchase multiple powers per Discipline level. My reasoning on this has to do with how certain Discipline levels split powers: Potence, for instance, treats learning how to do a super-powered jump as different from learning how to do a super-powered punch and... that doesn't quite make sense to me? I kind of get it from a game design perspective- they want to make characters feel distinct even when they have the same Discipline spread- but I personally think I want to offer this as an option for my players. So my question is, how should I set the XP costs for that? </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. </span></span></span></div><b>NO COST ADJUSTMENT. </b><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Buying a new Discipline power costs the exact same as purchasing that Discipline level. The drawback here is that filling out low-level powers means putting off investment in the higher Discipline levels.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2. </span></span></span></div><b>EXPONENTIAL COST. </b><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The more extreme option, this would allow the character to purchase </span></span></span></div><i>powers </i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">at increasingly steep costs: So if you want to purchase a second Level 1 power, it's going to cost the same as purchasing Level 2; a third Level 1 power will cost as much as purchasing Level 3; and so on, and so on. This also has the secondary drawback of reducing the number of powers you can know per Discipline level is inverse to the level of the Discipline (i.e., 5 Level 1 powers and 1 level 5 power). </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">3. </span></span></span></div><b>FLAT RAISED COST. </b><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Purchasing additional powers at a Discipline cost as much as the Discipline level about it. The rationale here is that the first power you had an innate affinity for your first power at a particular Discipline level, and learning to use different applications of that Discipline's level costs a little bit more. </span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> This also means that you can only ever have 1 Level 5 power. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What do you guys think? Is there another way I can let my players have multiple powers per Discipline level without everyone winding up with the same exact powers spread?</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T07:25:53-07:00","id":1384838,"title":"","content":"So I would caution against giving too much XP I did this and we had to restart the chronicle within 6 months they advanced too quickly. Part of this is due to the value of a single die being higher than in chronicles because you only need a 6 to succeed on it rather than an 8. There is also several ways to reduce costs and gain XP that we started to implore and realized increasing XP wasn\u2019t really necessary.<br /> <br /> As far as multiple discipline levels exponential cost is how the book already does it. They just cap you at 5 powers. I would just allow them to buy the 5th dot multiple times once they hit the 5 power limit. Many of us do this already for elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T08:17:49-07:00","id":1384846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384826-homebrew-ideas-need-help-v5?p=1384838#post1384838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would caution against giving too much XP I did this and we had to restart the chronicle within 6 months they advanced too quickly. Part of this is due to the value of a single die being higher than in chronicles because you only need a 6 to succeed on it rather than an 8. There is also several ways to reduce costs and gain XP that we started to implore and realized increasing XP wasn\u2019t really necessary.<br /> <br /> As far as multiple discipline levels exponential cost is how the book already does it. They just cap you at 5 powers. I would just allow them to buy the 5th dot multiple times once they hit the 5 power limit. Many of us do this already for elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the reason why I'm debating giving XP a little bit more generously is that I plan on letting the game run in asynchronous real-time: events that cover the span of a few nights will get played out session by session, but then we'll fast-forward to the present, and abstract the time in-between as long-term rolls and stuff. Thank you for reminding me about the difference in what counts as a success, though. Maybe I'll just drop it to two XP per session, or one per session, one per major objective, and one per time skip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T08:42:10-07:00","id":1384848,"title":"","content":"yea we ended up at 1 XP per session and one for telling me how you worked towards your ambition or desire. So basically 2 per session. We finish a story every other session or so so I also give a story reward of 1 xp for that as well.<br /> <br /> My players descovered that dyscracia can reduce costs so they do projects to tailor the blood of mortals to try and get those bumps and I fully cut the cost of any advantage the characters take the time it work through a project on. With all of these methods we feel it pretty good with the amount of advancement we are going through.<br /> <br /> tbh it is more work on the ST and just not allowing the deceases in game but bumping the XP would work probably just as well. But with both together it is too fast.<br /> <br /> Another note on projects that I have seen, our players value advantages more since they tie them up getting projects done and since I cut the cost the cost of them when done through projects they alwasy have a project going ot try and get more advancement and save there XP for attributes/skills/power and so on. This also means when something in game happens to an advantage they don't feel cheated as it was free anyway and it also adds a level of &quot;F&quot;ing with other peoples projects or me driving plot with their projects getting messed with into our plots.<br /> <br /> All in all you know your players best and only you and your players can truly know what is too much or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:32:19-07:00","id":1384857,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm working off of the &quot;sanctity of Merits&quot; concept that CoD introduced: basically, if the story results in the players losing a dot in an Advantage permanently, they will get its XP cost refunded. They won't be able to turn around and spend in on the same Advantage again, but they can use it to improve something else. Maybe damage to a Haven gets them some new Allies and Contacts among the local Anarchs, since the attack was perpetrated by a someone in the Prince's graces. Going to have to play around with it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm going to hand out free dots in Advantages, I think I'm just going to say that Advantages can't be pulled out of thin air, you need to work for them, and if I think they've made a good effort on something, they can buy dots in an appropriate Advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:42:54-07:00","id":1384858,"title":"","content":"I like the sanctity of merits concept. was always a firm believer if you spent XP for it it should be insured in some manor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:43:58-07:00","id":1384859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384826-homebrew-ideas-need-help-v5?p=1384857#post1384857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I'm working off of the &quot;sanctity of Merits&quot; concept that CoD introduced: basically, if the story results in the players losing a dot in an Advantage permanently, they will get its XP cost refunded. They won't be able to turn around and spend in on the same Advantage again, but they can use it to improve something else. Maybe damage to a Haven gets them some new Allies and Contacts among the local Anarchs, since the attack was perpetrated by a someone in the Prince's graces. Going to have to play around with it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm going to hand out free dots in Advantages, I think I'm just going to say that Advantages can't be pulled out of thin air, you need to work for them, and if I think they've made a good effort on something, they can buy dots in an appropriate Advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 already covers that in a sidebar about if something changes or is eliminated in the story, those dots get rassigned to something else (either a new version of the same thing, such as a new Ally in a different area or something thematic, like if you lose the Vegan flaw but end up with Prey exclusion). But you still have to always invest the XP into the thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T11:40:19-07:00","id":1384880,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs\">I posted my houserule for this here</a>, if it helps at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:09:20-07:00","id":1384948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384826-homebrew-ideas-need-help-v5?p=1384859#post1384859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> V5 already covers that in a sidebar about if something changes or is eliminated in the story, those dots get rassigned to something else (either a new version of the same thing, such as a new Ally in a different area or something thematic, like if you lose the Vegan flaw but end up with Prey exclusion). But you still have to always invest the XP into the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must've missed that. I'm glad that the development team and I were thinking along parallel lines, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs\">I posted my houserule for this here</a><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">, if it helps at all.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Thank you, I quite like this!</span></span></div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}